# Coding Style

## Trust the composition root
- No `== null` / `ArgumentNullException` / `?.` “just in case” for DI-injected deps or Resources assets the factory always loads
- Missing assets/wiring should fail loudly (NRE), not soft-return
- Keep real control-flow checks: disposed flags, optional gameplay state (`weapon == null`), optional params (`viewCamera`)

## Comments
- Do not add narrating comments, summaries, or “backward compatible” notes
- Code and names should explain intent; delete agent/TODO noise when touching a file

## APIs
- Prefer explicit constructors and readonly fields over late `Initialize` + nullable Func providers when deps are known at create time
- Pass concrete `Player` / `PlayerCamera` / services instead of stacks of `Func<>` wrappers

## Commits
- Match repo style: `feat:` / `fix:` / short why-focused subject
- Only commit when the user asks

## Answers to the user
- Direct and concise; Russian if the user writes in Russian
- No long recaps of what you “will do”; show outcomes
